From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Wed, 1 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fbdev: open the framebuffer close-on-exec

mm_miner keeps /dev/fb0 open for the life of the process and starts
long-lived children (core_miner, asic_miner, udhcpc -b through
system()). Opened without O_CLOEXEC, every one of them inherits the
framebuffer and holds it after mm_miner exits.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/drivers/display/fb/lv_linux_fbdev.c
+++ b/src/drivers/display/fb/lv_linux_fbdev.c
@@ -127,7 +127,7 @@
     if(dsc->fbfd > 0) close(dsc->fbfd);
 
     /* Open the file for reading and writing*/
-    dsc->fbfd = open(dsc->devname, O_RDWR);
+    dsc->fbfd = open(dsc->devname, O_RDWR | O_CLOEXEC);
     if(dsc->fbfd == -1) {
         perror("Error: cannot open framebuffer device");
         return;
